A||||1||falconhulk||Inside door pockets||||1||
Z||000000||falconhulk||09-17-2001||12:04 PM||||My interior looks brand new. The only exception to this is that the side pockets on the doors have specks of black where the bluish vinal paint has come off.  It almost gives a dirty look.  I dont want to go through the hassle of pulling these panels and having them redyed.  Anyone know if its possible to just cut them off?  It seems that there is a backing behind them.  If this sounds stupid I agree.  Anyone have another idea?  Anyone know of a wipe on dye I could use without pulling the panel?  I have 5 cars and 2 are in pieces.  Running on very limited space.  I dont think I could convince my wife to take this car down a few days for this.  Thanks for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||09-17-2001||01:13 PM||||There are 6 plastic posts on the back of each pocket that go thru holes drilled in the door panel.  They are attached with nuts on the back of each post.  If you cut the posts off, you will have come up with an alternate mounting method when you decide to re-install the pockets...<BR>||||reg||1
